The cantarellalab homebrew tap provides a source for homebrew formulae used
to distribute the software projects we support:

plcurve
ridgerunner
tsnnls
knoodle

Continuous integration
----------------------

These formulae are tested via GitHub CI actions on macOS (Apple Silicon),
Ubuntu Linux (Homebrew on Linux), and Fedora and Rocky Linux 9 containers,
monthly and whenever newer versions of the source projects are released.

Each formula is audited (brew audit --strict), built from source, and
exercised with its test block. The C libraries (libplcurve and libtsnnls)
additionally get a C++ header-include smoke test, so their installed public
headers stay usable from C++ as well as C.

